  "instructions": [
    "Preheat your oven to 425°F (220°C).",
    "Peel and slice the onions into thin rings.",
    "In a large kazán-cauldron, heat the olive oil over medium heat.",
    "Add the sliced onions and cook, stirring occasionally, until they are dark golden brown and caramelized, about 30 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic, cumin, cayenne pepper (if using), and black pepper to the cauldron and cook for 1-2 minutes, stirring constantly.",
    "Sprinkle the Algerian spice blend over the onions and stir to combine.",
    "Add the water to the cauldron and bring the mixture to a simmer.",
    "Transfer the cauldron to the preheated oven and roast the tagine for 20-25 minutes, or until the onions are crispy and the liquid has thickened.",
    "Remove the cauldron from the oven and sprinkle the chopped parsley (if using) and crumbled feta cheese (if using) over the top.",
    "Drizzle the lemon juice over the tagine and serve hot."
  ],
